MSync for MagicWine's pinned Wine 11.0 runtime (LGPL-2.1-or-later)

Public implementation: Marc-Aurel Zent, Zebediah Figura, and CodeWeavers.
Design/original patch set: https://github.com/marzent/wine-msync
Wine 11 inproc-sync adaptation imported from the public CrossOver 26.1 mirror:
https://github.com/rnowak/wine-crossover-sources/tree/b4f3c510a1808e6e32fb99e9bc11fa46ccc207dc/wine

Apply after the Metal, mouse-pointer, WPAD and remote-Metal patches. The backend
uses Mach messages, shared memory and Darwin shared ulocks; this is not an
environment-only switch. Existing Wine 11 inproc-sync hooks cover events,
semaphores, mutexes, APC alerts, process/thread termination and server objects.
WINEMSYNC=0 retains normal wineserver synchronization. Client/server mode
mismatches are fatal. The rebuilt server and ntdll use protocol 932 together.

Local port adjustments: preserve MagicWine's native Metal ABI wrappers; use the
msync debug channel; refuse both startup mode mismatches; never close a shared
alert index as a Unix fd; make Mach initialization failures fatal; preserve
recursive/abandoned mutex state and wake restored objects on wait-all rollback;
publish abandonment after clearing recursion; reject semaphore count overflow;
check APCs before wait-all acquisition; fix partial wait registration cleanup;
wait for registration acknowledgment before reusing the per-thread wait word.
Shared mappings use stable demand-zero pointer tables with atomic page publication.
Process-owned cache references are tracked through authenticated server requests,
reclaimed at final process death, and released on the ordered Mach pump only by
kernel-audit-authenticated wineserver commands. Shared references use checked
32-bit counts in matching 32-byte slots, with an ordered free-slot list. Native
NtReleaseMutant returns the Windows previous-state value (1 - recursion count).
Generated protocol files are included; regenerate with perl tools/make_requests.
Upstream file copyright/license notices are retained. Original pinned public
inputs, their SHA-256 digests and COPYING.LIB accompany the offline source bundle.

